## Building locally

If you want to make local modifications to these images for development purposes or just to customize the logic:

```bash
git clone {{ repo_url }}.git
cd {{ repo }}
docker build \
  --no-cache \
  --pull \
  -t {{ image_ref }} .
```

The ARM variants can be built on x86_64 hardware and vice versa using `ghcr.io/{{ settings.upstream_org }}/qemu-static`

```bash
docker run --rm --privileged ghcr.io/{{ settings.upstream_org }}/qemu-static --reset
```

Once registered you can define the dockerfile to use with `-f Dockerfile.aarch64`.

Every push builds and tests the image with the shared workflow in [`{{ org }}/workflows`](https://github.com/{{ org }}/workflows); every build's tests, screenshots and package changes are on [the image's builds]({{ builds_page_url }}) on the website.
